---
import SupportLayout from '../../layouts/SupportLayout.astro';
---
<SupportLayout title="Privacy Policy" eyebrow="SUPPORT / PRIVACY" description="What information we collect, why we use it, and how you can manage your information.">
  <h2>1. Who operates this website</h2>
  <p>This website is operated for Perennial Fallout, a music group. For privacy questions, requests for access or deletion, or concerns about information you have provided, contact <a class="support-email" href="mailto:perennialfallout@gmail.com?subject=Privacy%20Request">perennialfallout@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
  <p>When you subscribe to the newsletter, we collect the email address you submit and records needed to manage your consent, including subscription status, when confirmation was requested, and when the address was confirmed or unsubscribed. We use one-time verification tokens to help prevent unauthorized subscriptions.</p>
  <p>If you click Buy Track, you leave this website for the Perennial Fallout Fourthwall storefront homepage. If you choose to purchase an available product there, Fourthwall handles the order, customer details, payment processing, and digital delivery under its own privacy policy and terms. This website does not collect payment-card details. We may receive order-related information from Fourthwall to provide purchaser support.</p>
  <p>When you contact the band by email, we receive the information you include in your message. Our hosting and anti-abuse services may process technical information, such as IP addresses, browser data, and requests, to deliver the website, protect forms from abuse, and diagnose errors. Our newsletter provider processes email delivery information such as delivery and bounce status.</p>
  <p>If you choose to remember music player preferences, your browser stores the selected volume and repeat settings on your device. You can disable or erase those preferences from <a href="/cookie-preferences/">Cookie Preferences</a>.</p>
  <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To send a one-time subscription confirmation and confirm that you control the address.</li>
    <li>To maintain a list of people who have explicitly confirmed an interest in future band email updates.</li>
    <li>To send a subscription welcome or status message and notify the band of a confirmed signup.</li>
    <li>To respond to inquiries, operate the site, and prevent fraudulent or automated signups.</li>
    <li>To preserve your unsubscribe choice so we do not continue sending unwanted marketing messages.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The website's current newsletter code sends confirmation and welcome messages, not ongoing marketing campaigns. If the band begins sending newsletters, they should be sent only to confirmed subscribers with an unsubscribe option. We do not sell the email subscriber list.</p>
  <h2>4. Service providers and links</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare. When the newsletter service is configured, Cloudflare Turnstile helps prevent automated signups, Cloudflare D1 stores subscription records, and Resend sends confirmation and welcome emails. Confirmed-signup notifications can be sent to the band's Gmail address. The homepage and support pages may request fonts from Google Fonts; the EPK serves its fonts locally.</p>
  <p>These companies may process the information needed to provide their services under their own service terms and privacy notices. Links to Fourthwall, social platforms, ticketing sites, and other music services are operated by third parties and have separate privacy policies.</p>
  <h2>5. Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>The supplied website code does not include advertising pixels or optional analytics trackers. This statement does not cover any additional settings independently enabled by the hosting or storefront providers. It uses local storage to record privacy preferences, and it can optionally remember music playback settings if you enable that feature. Essential security services and external font requests may process technical browser information. Read the details and manage your choices on our <a href="/cookie-preferences/">Cookie Preferences</a> page.</p>
  <h2>6. Retention and security</h2>
  <p>We keep active subscriber records while a subscription remains in effect, and we retain limited suppression or status information as reasonably needed to honor unsubscribe requests and document subscription choices. Unconfirmed addresses may be deleted during periodic maintenance. Emails and records held by service providers may be retained under their applicable schedules. We use appropriate access restrictions and secure hosting, but no online system can guarantee absolute security.</p>
  <h2>7. Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
  <p>You can decline to subscribe, ignore a confirmation email, or unsubscribe using the link included in subscription messages. You may also request access to, correction of, or deletion of information associated with your email by contacting <a class="support-email" href="mailto:perennialfallout@gmail.com?subject=Privacy%20Request">perennialfallout@gmail.com</a>. We may need to verify that you control the email address before fulfilling a request. Some limited data may be kept when legally required or reasonably needed to honor an opt-out.</p>
  <p>If applicable privacy laws give you additional rights, including rights to access, delete, correct, or limit certain processing, you can exercise those rights through the same contact address. We do not discriminate against people for exercising privacy rights.</p>
  <h2>8. Children</h2>
  <p>This site is intended for a general music audience and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has submitted personal information, contact us so it can be reviewed and removed as appropriate.</p>
  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy as the website's features or providers change. The updated date on this page shows when it was last revised. Material changes to how subscriber information is used will be reflected here before the new use begins.</p>
  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy inquiries: <a class="support-email" href="mailto:perennialfallout@gmail.com?subject=Privacy%20Request">perennialfallout@gmail.com</a></p>
</SupportLayout>
